# Exercise 2: Your first rule
#
# A rule says when something is true, based on other things:
#
#     rule happy(x):
#         likes(x, "sunshine")
#
# means "x is happy if x likes sunshine". The name x is a variable: it can
# stand for anyone. A variable is written without quotes.
#
# Below are parent facts: parent("Ada", "Ben") means Ada is a parent of Ben.
#
# Your task: write a rule child(c, p) that is true when c is a child of p.
# (Think about what parent fact has to be true for that.)

fact parent("Ada", "Ben")
fact parent("Ada", "Fay")
fact parent("Ben", "Cy")

# Write your rule below this line.



# --- Checks: run ./sova --check on this file. Don't change below here. ---
hint "c is a child of p exactly when p is a parent of c."
hint "The rule has one goal: parent(p, c). Notice the order of the variables."
expect child("Ben", "Ada")
expect child("Cy", "Ben")
expect NOT child("Ada", "Ben")
expect child(who, "Ada") gives "Ben", "Fay"
expect child("Cy", p) gives "Ben"
